Set
A set is a collection of unique values.

Properties
- No duplicate elements
- Order is not guaranteed
- Fast membership checking.
Example: {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}

When sets are useful
- checking if an element already exists
- removing duplicates
- fast membership checks
- tracking visited elements in graph problems

HashSet
A HashSet is an implementation of a set using hashing
Iinternally it works similarly to a HashMap but only stores keys.

Operations:
add(x)
remove(x)
contains(x)

Time Complexity (Average)
Insert: O(1)
Lookup: O(1)
Delete: O(1)

Typical Uses:
- Contains Duplicate
- Longest Consecutive Sequence
- Visited tracking in graph traversal.